Subject: [PATCH 20/23] refactor: rewire main.py onto
 broker.factory.get_gateway
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces direct core.mt5_connection/core.market_data.MarketData calls
with broker.factory.get_gateway(settings) — main.py no longer imports
MetaTrader5 or any broker-specific module. run() is now async (entered
via asyncio.run in main()) to use the gateway's async interface, and
uses 'async with gateway:' so disconnect is always called.

Same behavior otherwise: still stops after market analysis (regime
detection) with the Milestone 1 warning about signal/risk/execution
not being wired in yet — this refactor only changes how market data is
sourced, not what's done with it.

Tests updated for the async, gateway-based flow (mocking get_gateway's
return value instead of individual MT5 calls).
---
 main.py | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------------------
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

diff --git a/main.py b/main.py
index e65063d..7e35862 100644
--- a/main.py
